Lexifina's own contributions to this repository (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables,
the documentation and the tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

The legal texts are official texts of the Republic of Senegal (and, in actes-communautaires/ and traites/,
instruments of UEMOA, CEDEAO, OHADA and other organisations as printed in the Journal officiel). They come from:

- Journal officiel de la République du Sénégal, web edition (www.jo.gouv.sn, 2001-2018), read from Internet
  Archive captures (https://web.archive.org/web/*/www.jo.gouv.sn/*); the site read "© Copyrights Gouvernement du
  Sénégal" and stated no licence.
- Conseil constitutionnel du Sénégal (https://conseilconstitutionnel.sn/la-loi-organique/), "© Copyright 2026. tous
  droits réservés"; no licence stated for the legal texts.
- Vie Publique Sénégal (https://www.vie-publique.sn), civic publisher; its robots.txt carries
  "Content-Signal: search=yes, ai-input=yes, ai-train=no, use=reference". The texts taken are the official PDFs it
  hosts (laws, ordinances, decrees; the Code des douanes as published by the Direction générale des douanes).
- Commission de Protection des Données Personnelles (cdp.sn, Internet Archive copy), for two words of Loi n° 2008-12.

None of these publishers states a licence for the legal texts; their copyright status is not confirmed here, and
they are reproduced as official texts with the attribution above. Changes made by Lexifina: one Markdown file per
provision, one paragraph per line; spacing, apostrophes and broken encodings normalised; headings, exposés des
motifs, visas, signatures and executory formulas removed. The wording of the law was not otherwise changed. None of
the publishers endorses this repository.
